// Single-action schema, `since` flavor: with only one action, both arms of
// a `since` must be field-refinements of the SAME action. "Permit a
// transfer only if every transfer since the last big one (amount 100) was
// small (amount 1)." Per the guide's semantics, `left since within W right`
// holds iff some anchor j in the window has `right`, and `left` holds at
// every k in [j+1, i] — reflexively true at the anchor itself (empty range).
//
// Trace (all alice): big(@0), small(@10), small(@20), medium(@30), small(@40).
// tp0: anchor j=0 (amount 100), [j+1, 0] empty        -> true
// tp1: anchor j=0, left holds at tp1                  -> true
// tp2: anchor j=0, left holds at tp1..tp2             -> true
// tp3: left fails at tp3 (amount 5); no other anchor  -> false
// tp4: left fails at tp3 in [1, 4]; no other anchor   -> false

permit (
    principal,
    action == Drupe::Action::"Transfer",
    resource
)
when temporal {
    Drupe::Action::"Transfer"::request{ input.amount: 1 }
    since within 1h
    Drupe::Action::"Transfer"::request{ input.amount: 100 }
};
